equalBettiTally -- Computes the Betti table of two modules and compares for equality
************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        equalBettiTally(M,N)
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, 
      * N, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 

Description
===========

+------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = QQ[a..f];                  |
+------------------------------------+
|i2 : m = matrix{{a,b,d,e},{b,c,e,f}}|
|                                    |
|o2 = | a b d e |                    |
|     | b c e f |                    |
|                                    |
|             2      4               |
|o2 : Matrix S  <-- S                |
+------------------------------------+
|i3 : M = coker m                    |
|                                    |
|o3 = cokernel | a b d e |           |
|              | b c e f |           |
|                                    |
|                            2       |
|o3 : S-module, quotient of S        |
+------------------------------------+
|i4 : n = matrix{{a,b},{c,d},{e,f}}  |
|                                    |
|o4 = | a b |                        |
|     | c d |                        |
|     | e f |                        |
|                                    |
|             3      2               |
|o4 : Matrix S  <-- S                |
+------------------------------------+
|i5 : N = coker n                    |
|                                    |
|o5 = cokernel | a b |               |
|              | c d |               |
|              | e f |               |
|                                    |
|                            3       |
|o5 : S-module, quotient of S        |
+------------------------------------+
|i6 : equalBettiTally(M,N)           |
|                                    |
|o6 = false                          |
+------------------------------------+

